WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.860
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 9. Topic: Frequency Distribution & Mean. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:18.946
The frequency distribution table and the cumulative frequency distribution table below show the distribution of the weights of 20 apples.

3
00:00:19.106 --> 00:00:40.252
Weight (grams) Frequency 91 minus 100 2 101 minus 110 a 111 minus 120 6 121 minus 130 7 131 minus 140 h Weight less than (grams) Cumulative frequency 100.5 2 110.5 6.

4
00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:51.569
120.5 12 130.5 b 140.5 k (a) Find a and b. (b) Find the mean of the distribution.

5
00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:56.210
Step 1. PART (a) — find a.

6
00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:03.809
Key rule: Cumulative Frequency. cumulative frequency equals sum of the frequencies up to that class.

7
00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:09.596
The first two classes hold 2 plus a apples, and the table states this total is 6.

8
00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:18.991
The cumulative frequency at 110.5 equals the frequencies of the first two classes: 2 plus a equals 6 which gives a equals 4.

9
00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:23.867
Step 2. PART (a) — find b.

10
00:01:24.027 --> 00:01:34.854
The cumulative frequency at 130.5 equals the sum of the first four frequencies: b equals 2 plus 4 plus 6 plus 7 equals 19 (Consistency.

11
00:01:35.014 --> 00:01:44.073
since there are 20 apples, k equals 20 and h equals 20 minus 19 equals 1, which matches the last row of the cumulative table.).

12
00:01:44.493 --> 00:01:50.069
Step 3. PART (b) — mean using class midpoints.

13
00:01:50.229 --> 00:02:04.037
Key rule: Mean from a Frequency Table. x equals the sum of fx over the sum of f. With midpoints 95 to 135 and 20 apples, the total 2310 gives the mean.

14
00:02:04.197 --> 00:02:12.996
Midpoints: 95, 105, 115, 125, 135.

15
00:02:13.156 --> 00:02:36.188
Mean equals 2(95) plus 4(105) plus 6(115) plus 7(125) plus 1(135) over 20 equals 190 plus 420 plus 690 plus 875 plus 135 over 20 equals 2310 over 20.

16
00:02:36.608 --> 00:02:45.419
So the answer is: (a) a equals 4, b equals 19 (b) Mean equals 115.5 grams.

17
00:02:45.839 --> 00:02:54.693
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 9. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
